  "title": "AudioProcessorValueTreeState Patterns",
  "summary": "JUCE parameter management using APVTS for thread-safe parameter access",
  "description": "AudioProcessorValueTreeState (APVTS) is JUCE's solution for thread-safe parameter management in audio plugins. It provides a single source of truth for all parameters, atomic access from the audio thread, and automatic UI binding. Key patterns: use createParameterLayout() to define parameters, getRawParameterValue() returns std::atomic<float>* for RT-safe reads, SliderAttachment/ButtonAttachment for UI binding without manual listeners, and getStateInformation()/setStateInformation() for state serialization. Never call parameter setValue() from processBlock—use atomic pointers instead.",
  "source": {
    "type": "framework-docs",
    "reference": "research/best-practices.md#parameter-management-apvts-pattern",
    "url": "https://docs.juce.com/master/tutorial_audio_processor_value_tree_state.html"
  },
