  "title": "Psybient Sound Design Techniques",
  "summary": "Slow evolving textures, ethnic elements, atmospheric soundscapes at 60-100 BPM",
  "description": "Psybient (psychedelic ambient) combines atmospheric soundscapes with rhythmic elements at downtempo speeds (60-100 BPM). Key techniques: asynchronous modulation uses multiple LFOs at different, unsynced rates (e.g., 0.07 Hz, 0.13 Hz, 15-sec envelope cycle) creating sounds that evolve naturally and almost never repeat. Granular freezing holds a single position with jitter/spray for organic variation. Recursive reverb feeds reflections back for harmonic excavation. Worldizing plays sounds through physical spaces and re-records. Layered saturation adds harmonics to dark pads. Core characteristics: slow tempo, atmospheric textures with layered synths, ethnic/world influences (flutes, tribal sounds, field recordings), spiritual/meditative focus, evolving sounds rather than aggressive peaks.",
  "source": {
    "type": "expert-tutorial",
    "reference": "research/best-practices.md#psychedelic-ambient-psybient-techniques",
